Error [jet.UnknownCasingStyle]: `#Rename(.Shouty)` on a type isn't a known casing style.
  --> tests/ui/serde_rename_case_bad_style.jet:3:19
    |
  3 | #[Codable, Rename(.Shouty)]
    |                   ^^^^^^^
 Why: On a type, `#Rename` sets the wire casing of every field or variant from the closed NamingCase menu `.Camel`/`.Snake`/`.Pascal`/`.Kebab`/`.Screaming`; anything else is rejected so a typo fails at compile time, not on the wire. A string name renames one field or variant.
 Fix: Pick one of `.Camel` / `.Snake` / `.Pascal` / `.Kebab` / `.Screaming`, or move a string `#Rename` onto the field or variant it names.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2409
